Input: {"question": "What is the primary function of the Butterfly House?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 0, "end": 56, "text": "Butterfly House, Missouri Botanical Garden The Sophia M."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 57, "end": 209, "text": "Sachs Butterfly House is a butterfly zoo operated by the Missouri Botanical Gardens, and located in Faust Park in Chesterfield, Missouri, United States."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 210, "end": 291, "text": "The Butterfly House is accredited by the Association of Zoos and Aquariums (AZA)."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 292, "end": 425, "text": "Ground was broken for the Butterfly House in June 1997, and The Butterfly House opened its doors to the public on September 18, 1998."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 426, "end": 495, "text": "In 2000 the outdoor area known as the Butterfly Garden was dedicated."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 496, "end": 582, "text": "In July, 2001, the Butterfly House became a division of the Missouri Botanical Garden."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d00", "start": 583, "end": 622, "text": "In 2002, the \"Emerson Lakeside Terrace\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d01", "start": 0, "end": 7, "text": "living."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d01", "start": 8, "end": 172, "text": "Due to the increased availability of family cars, a sheltered parking space is included underneath the cantilevered floor resulting in ease of access for residents."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d01", "start": 173, "end": 299, "text": "The Butterfly House is one of the earliest examples in Australia to use prefabricated structural steel in a domestic building."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d01", "start": 300, "end": 434, "text": "The structural core consists of two triangulated truss frames, bolted to large concrete footings at the inverted tip of the triangles."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d01", "start": 435, "end": 564, "text": "Steel ‘C’ section purlins and steel cross bracing form the base of the first floor, tying the triangulated truss frames together."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d01", "start": 565, "end": 636, "text": "The two dominant floor beams overlap the first floor truss supporting a"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d02", "start": 0, "end": 71, "text": "a similar effect to using a prism to split white light into a rainbow ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d02", "start": 72, "end": 224, "text": "Diffractive scales give off brilliant metallic and iridescent colours , and do not fade over time because they have no pigment chemicals to break down ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d02", "start": 225, "end": 297, "text": "Androconia scales are scales that produce pheromones instead of colour ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d02", "start": 298, "end": 482, "text": "Pheromones are chemicals that butterflies release into the air to communicate with other butterflies of the same species , and are usually involved in helping butterflies find a mate ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d02", "start": 483, "end": 563, "text": "A butterfly ’ s wings are used for flight , but also have many other functions ."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d02", "start": 564, "end": 572, "text": "Patterns"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d03", "start": 0, "end": 120, "text": "the first of its kind in the US to concentrate on native species butterflies and is still one of very few that does so ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d03", "start": 121, "end": 234, "text": "Most other facilities are year-round indoor facilities which house both tropical and native species butterflies ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d03", "start": 235, "end": 421, "text": "Instead of focusing on exotic species , the Paul Smith ’ s College VIC Butterfly House reflects what is really happening in the Adirondack Park , at the exact time that it is happening ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d03", "start": 422, "end": 547, "text": "All insects in the Butterfly House are collected by VIC volunteers from the immediate area or raised in the Butterfly House ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0222-caca15eed405:d03", "start": 548, "end": 555, "text": "Is this"}}, "candidates": [], "original_cards": [], "initial_answers": []}

